<title>USA: Wash. Water Power says storm cost $10-15 mln.</title>
<headline>Wash. Water Power says storm cost $10-15 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Washington Water Power Co estimated Thursday it cost $10 million to $15 million to repair damage to the company's electric system caused by an ice storm last month.</p>
<p>Paul Redmond, WWP chairman, said the costs will be written off against fourth-quarter 1996 earnings.</p>
<p>&quot;Make no mistake, this natural disaster has caused a significant financial loss for our company,&quot; Redmond said. Redmond estimated that the impact on company earnings would be in the range of $0.08-$0.14 per share on an after-tax basis. He said there is no insurance coverage available to cover this type of storm.</p>
</text>
